sequenceDiagram
    autonumber off
    actor Admin
    actor Steward
    participant Loader as Geometry load job<br/>loadGeometriesFromKml (proposed)
    participant KML as Alberta government KML<br/>(same source as website)
    participant DB as Supabase DB<br/>sites_pa, kml_sites
    participant Pages as Map and admin pages
    participant Geo as /api/geocode route
    participant OC as OpenCage API

    Note over Admin,OC: Covers US 6.0.1. sites_pa has no geometry columns today.<br/>"(proposed)" = the step is not in the code today.<br/>Open question: load the KML into a table or read the file each time. kml_sites is the proposed option.

    Admin->>Loader: Start geometry load (proposed)
    Loader->>Loader: Check caller is Admin from a trusted role source, store not decided (proposed)
    alt Caller is not Admin
        Loader-->>Admin: Refuse (403). Nothing is loaded
    else Caller is Admin
        Loader->>KML: Download KML file
        KML-->>Loader: Placemarks with boundaries
        Loader->>DB: Store every placemark in kml_sites:<br/>source_feature_id, name, boundary, loaded_at (proposed)
        Loader->>DB: Read active sites_pa rows
        DB-->>Loader: Active sites
        loop Each active site
            Loader->>Loader: Match site name to a placemark
            alt Match is found
                Loader->>DB: Set source_feature_id, boundary as in the KML,<br/>and centre point (lat, lng) on the site (AT 1, AT 2)
            else No match
                Loader->>Loader: Leave source_feature_id NULL (AT 3)
            end
        end
        Loader-->>Admin: Report matched and unmatched counts
    end
    Admin->>Pages: Open unmatched sites list (proposed)
    Pages->>DB: Read active sites_pa rows<br/>where source_feature_id IS NULL
    DB-->>Pages: Unmatched sites (the AT 3 list)
    Pages-->>Admin: Show sites for an Admin to fix

    opt A site has no point and fallback geocoding is used (AT 4)
        Pages->>Geo: GET /api/geocode?q=site name (exists)
        Geo->>Geo: Look for a cached result for this name (proposed)
        alt Cached result exists
            Geo-->>Pages: lat, lng from the cache. No OpenCage request
        else No cached result
            Geo->>Geo: Read the OpenCage request count for today (proposed)
            alt Count has reached the daily limit of 2,500
                Geo-->>Pages: No result. No OpenCage request
            else Count is less than the limit
                Geo->>OC: Geocode request. Add 1 to the count for today (proposed)
                alt External API returns a result
                    OC-->>Geo: lat, lng
                    Geo->>Geo: Store the result in the cache (proposed)
                    Geo-->>Pages: lat, lng
                else External API refuses the request or its quota is exhausted
                    OC-->>Geo: Error or no result
                    Geo-->>Pages: No result
                end
            end
        end
    end

    Steward->>Pages: Open the map
    Pages->>DB: Read site boundary and centre point (AT 2)
    DB-->>Pages: Geometry
    Pages-->>Steward: Draw site on the map

    Note over Pages,OC: Open question: where the geocode cache and the daily request count are stored,<br/>for example a database table or server memory. The proposed ER diagram does not show them yet.<br/>StewardLog calls OpenCage separately from the phone. If it uses the same key, its requests also count.
